s would redefine the balance of power in the Holy Land. The city’s historical relevance is further underscored by its role as a cultural hub for Sunni Arabs, serving as the administrative center of the Saladin Governorate, thereby influencing the sociopolitical landscape of Iraq and the surrounding region.

